cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these scripts, data or results, please cite the paper."
title: >-
  Detecting Data Contamination in Large Language Models: A Comparison of
  Question-Level and Evidence-Level Perturbations
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Ximing
    affiliation: "NUIST Waterford Institute, Nanjing University of Information Science and Technology"
year: 2026
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a controlled canary suite that tests whether black-box
  perturbation invariance detects data contamination in large language models.
  The release contains the suite generators and validator, the API and local
  evaluation harnesses, all raw per-item results, and the scripts that regenerate
  the paper's tables and figures.
keywords:
  - data contamination
  - benchmark contamination
  - memorisation
  - black-box evaluation
  - large language models
